(3562338, 498967, 67152, '<td valign="top">i like the effort here to try something a little different from the DPC standard fare - the grain is pretty good except for a few small areas in the sky that appear a little blotchy.  <br/> <br/>I think having the path not run directly off to the side would have helped ''the story'' of this image - it appears almost too abrupt as it currently runs away so hard to the right</td>', 'i like the effort here to try something a little different from the DPC standard fare - the grain is pretty good except for a few small areas in the sky that appear a little blotchy.   I think having the path not run directly off to the side would have helped ''the story'' of this image - it appears almost too abrupt as it currently runs away so hard to the right', '2007-04-19 08:48:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3562343, 499295, 67152, '<td valign="top">this image seems a little static - likely due to the placement of the horizion almost dead center.  there was a great sky above you and it might have been wise to cut off the fence in front and bring out more of the sky above.</td>', 'this image seems a little static - likely due to the placement of the horizion almost dead center.  there was a great sky above you and it might have been wise to cut off the fence in front and bring out more of the sky above.', '2007-04-19 08:54:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(3562350, 496990, 65886, '<td valign="top">wonderful! the bird and the tree (?) are excellent! cool lighting, too<br/>bumping from 8 to 10 after viewing all the entries.<br/>the lighting is not just cool, it is excellent.<br/>it looks like your used some special shooting method, but i don''t know much about them and can''t say what exactly it is.<br/>do you get comments saying the horizon line should be straight?:)<br/>it is one of the finest examples of real fine art I have seen. I would like to have it on the wall, really.</td>', 'wonderful! the bird and the tree (?) are excellent! cool lighting, toobumping from 8 to 10 after viewing all the entries.the lighting is not just cool, it is excellent.it looks like your used some special shooting method, but i don''t know much about them and can''t say what exactly it is.do you get comments saying the horizon line should be straight?:)it is one of the finest examples of real fine art I have seen. I would like to have it on the wall, really.', '2007-04-19 09:01:54.000000', NULL, 1),
