(3565912, 499030, 39679, '<td valign="top">Not sure why it''s forbidden but it''s a very nice shot.</td>', 'Not sure why it''s forbidden but it''s a very nice shot.', '2007-04-20 12:34:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3565918, 499352, 39679, '<td valign="top">Really nice shot.  Great use of DOF to help with the sense of distance.</td>', 'Really nice shot.  Great use of DOF to help with the sense of distance.', '2007-04-20 12:36:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(3565920, 499241, 39679, '<td valign="top">I would normally think this too dark but it makes the lighting even more interesting.  Great shot.</td>', 'I would normally think this too dark but it makes the lighting even more interesting.  Great shot.', '2007-04-20 12:37:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(3565923, 498955, 39679, '<td valign="top">Shooting falling snow is tough.  To me the snow flakes always look like dust on the lens.  Still a nice shot.</td>', 'Shooting falling snow is tough.  To me the snow flakes always look like dust on the lens.  Still a nice shot.', '2007-04-20 12:38:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(3565928, 499000, 39679, '<td valign="top">Nice use of post production.  It really enhances an already great shot.  Subtlety too often is lost when people open Photoshop.</td>', 'Nice use of post production.  It really enhances an already great shot.  Subtlety too often is lost when people open Photoshop.', '2007-04-20 12:39:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(3565943, 498938, 39679, '<td valign="top">Nicely exposed</td>', 'Nicely exposed', '2007-04-20 12:44:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(3565962, 497523, 39679, '<td valign="top">This is a really interesting shot...right up to the rock in the foreground - it''s distracting and doesn''t add to the image.  I''ve love to see this shot again but zoomed in closer.  The clouds are awesome.</td>', 'This is a really interesting shot...right up to the rock in the foreground - it''s distracting and doesn''t add to the image.  I''ve love to see this shot again but zoomed in closer.  The clouds are awesome.', '2007-04-20 12:50:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(3565966, 499253, 39679, '<td valign="top">I''m glad you shot this from below (probably didn''t have much of a choice huh?).  It really makes the outcroping look huge.  Nicely done.</td>', 'I''m glad you shot this from below (probably didn''t have much of a choice huh?).  It really makes the outcroping look huge.  Nicely done.', '2007-04-20 12:51:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3565978, 496409, 39679, '<td valign="top">Monochrome, particularly off sepia, really doesn''t suit this image.  You should be careful about using monochrome when it doesn''t add something to the image.</td>', 'Monochrome, particularly off sepia, really doesn''t suit this image.  You should be careful about using monochrome when it doesn''t add something to the image.', '2007-04-20 12:56:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(3565981, 497046, 39679, '<td valign="top">Polarizers are great (and, in this case, really make the clouds stand out) but keep in mind what they do to exposure.  IMHO, this image is just a tad dark.</td>', 'Polarizers are great (and, in this case, really make the clouds stand out) but keep in mind what they do to exposure.  IMHO, this image is just a tad dark.', '2007-04-20 12:58:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566063, 498329, 77328, '<td valign="top">I am a sucker for B/W photos. I like this one! I love the symmetry of the posts and play of the shadows on them. NICE!</td>', 'I am a sucker for B/W photos. I like this one! I love the symmetry of the posts and play of the shadows on them. NICE!', '2007-04-20 13:36:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566072, 499119, 77328, '<td valign="top">Being Dutch I obviously am prejudice to this....! I love the colors. The use of the "Thirds Rule" is excellently executed. Really good. (P.S. Is this in Holland?).</td>', 'Being Dutch I obviously am prejudice to this....! I love the colors. The use of the "Thirds Rule" is excellently executed. Really good. (P.S. Is this in Holland?).', '2007-04-20 13:39:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566081, 498942, 77328, '<td valign="top">I like the compostion of the image and the olors. However, it seems that the details in the rocks have been lost. I would have liked to see a little bit more detail in the texture......</td>', 'I like the compostion of the image and the olors. However, it seems that the details in the rocks have been lost. I would have liked to see a little bit more detail in the texture......', '2007-04-20 13:44:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566084, 499156, 15330, '<td valign="top">Great depth, really like the use of wide angle to show the foreground. Increasing brightness, and contrast on everything but the sky, and mountain should help this photo.</td>', 'Great depth, really like the use of wide angle to show the foreground. Increasing brightness, and contrast on everything but the sky, and mountain should help this photo.', '2007-04-20 13:45:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566110, 499257, 15330, '<td valign="top">This photo would benifit from increased contrast. There are no true blacks, or whites, everything is grey.</td>', 'This photo would benifit from increased contrast. There are no true blacks, or whites, everything is grey.', '2007-04-20 13:57:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566112, 498814, 56880, '<td valign="top">The lone (rock?, person? sea-monster?) on the beach, watching the waves, grey skies.. I thought "solitude" before I read the title.</td>', 'The lone (rock?, person? sea-monster?) on the beach, watching the waves, grey skies.. I thought "solitude" before I read the title.', '2007-04-20 13:58:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566114, 496414, 73121, '<td valign="top">Really nice waterfall with good surrounding color.  The highlight sky is my only complaint, a bit of a distraction.  Good shot.</td>', 'Really nice waterfall with good surrounding color.  The highlight sky is my only complaint, a bit of a distraction.  Good shot.', '2007-04-20 13:58:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566118, 498343, 56880, '<td valign="top">Spectacular!  I''m sure you''ll get all kinds of comments about how well everything is lit..  The marina in the foreground provides a depth often lacking in lightning captures.</td>', 'Spectacular!  I''m sure you''ll get all kinds of comments about how well everything is lit..  The marina in the foreground provides a depth often lacking in lightning captures.', '2007-04-20 14:00:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566122, 499140, 73121, '<td valign="top">Really nice golden color you captured in the trees/light.  This reminds me a lot of Oklahoma:)</td>', 'Really nice golden color you captured in the trees/light.  This reminds me a lot of Oklahoma:)', '2007-04-20 14:01:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566125, 497963, 73121, '<td valign="top">I like the pp on this, almost a painting feel to it.  I also like the curve to the shoreline.</td>', 'I like the pp on this, almost a painting feel to it.  I also like the curve to the shoreline.', '2007-04-20 14:02:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566129, 497574, 77354, '<td valign="top">too much filter</td>', 'too much filter', '2007-04-20 14:04:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566131, 499204, 77354, '<td valign="top">it looks fake</td>', 'it looks fake', '2007-04-20 14:04:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566133, 497901, 77354, '<td valign="top">color is not sharp enough</td>', 'color is not sharp enough', '2007-04-20 14:05:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(3566142, 498887, 77250, '<td valign="top">The water in this image looks incredible.  The tones and colors are perfect since the exposure was right on.  I do think, however, that the sky is quite blown out.  A split ND filter would have helped in this scene.  The other thing that you could have done was shot in RAW and processed two seperate exposures: one for the sky and one for the water.  Then you could have combined the two images into on using the sky from one and the water from the other.  That would have made a perfect exposure where the sky and the water are equally dynamic.  I still gave you a seven on this shot since the scene is so beautiful and the composition is right on.</td>', 'The water in this image looks incredible.  The tones and colors are perfect since the exposure was right on.  I do think, however, that the sky is quite blown out.  A split ND filter would have helped in this scene.  The other thing that you could have done was shot in RAW and processed two seperate exposures: one for the sky and one for the water.  Then you could have combined the two images into on using the sky from one and the water from the other.  That would have made a perfect exposure where the sky and the water are equally dynamic.  I still gave you a seven on this shot since the scene is so beautiful and the composition is right on.', '2007-04-20 14:08:05.000000', NULL, 1),
