(3579293, 498327, 27133, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aerogurl:</b></div><hr/><i> First of all, this is not a landscape, its a seascape. Its overprocessed and DNMC. It is a beautiful image tho. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That is your call.  There is land within the shot.  It is a landscape.  But that is my opinion......not yours.  I respect your vote of 1, I don''t agree with it...but I do respect your choice.</td>', 'Originally posted by aerogurl: First of all, this is not a landscape, its a seascape. Its overprocessed and DNMC. It is a beautiful image tho.   That is your call.  There is land within the shot.  It is a landscape.  But that is my opinion......not yours.  I respect your vote of 1, I don''t agree with it...but I do respect your choice.', '2007-04-25 01:02:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3579295, 498122, 69102, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! Love it when my favorite wins the blue. Very well deserved.</td>', 'Congratulations! Love it when my favorite wins the blue. Very well deserved.', '2007-04-25 01:02:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3579296, 498327, 27133, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by TIHadi:</b></div><hr/><i> The volume light is going in too many directions!! The wave should break from behind the girl same direction of the waves. The colors of the sky do not match. poor job of mixing the breaking wave with the clouds above it.<br/>The light on the bird is coming from the wrong direction.<br/>Powerful editing tools in the wrong hands. 1 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You are so wrong.  The entire image except for the mermaid was taken at the same time looking in the same direction.  There are 3 images in there...all at different exposures but all from the same spot on the sand and the same time frame.  The water splashing was as it shows....not swapped from another side.<br/> <br/>The mermaid shot was taken on a rock 5 meters to the left of this one but facing the land.  So she was between the land and myself on a rock that is about 6 foot tall.  That rock was completely underwater in the splashing shot.  but the lighting was the same for all images. <br/> <br/>Maybe I don''t know how to use PS.  But at least I try.  You get upset over someone giving you a one...well I think you need to explain to the public why you felt that my image was so poorly done that it only deserved a one.  <br/> <br/>I personally would like to challenge you to a showdown of the same technique and conditions.  Put your money where your mouth is.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by TIHadi: The volume light is going in too many directions!! The wave should break from behind the girl same direction of the waves. The colors of the sky do not match. poor job of mixing the breaking wave with the clouds above it.The light on the bird is coming from the wrong direction.Powerful editing tools in the wrong hands. 1   You are so wrong.  The entire image except for the mermaid was taken at the same time looking in the same direction.  There are 3 images in there...all at different exposures but all from the same spot on the sand and the same time frame.  The water splashing was as it shows....not swapped from another side. The mermaid shot was taken on a rock 5 meters to the left of this one but facing the land.  So she was between the land and myself on a rock that is about 6 foot tall.  That rock was completely underwater in the splashing shot.  but the lighting was the same for all images.  Maybe I don''t know how to use PS.  But at least I try.  You get upset over someone giving you a one...well I think you need to explain to the public why you felt that my image was so poorly done that it only deserved a one.   I personally would like to challenge you to a showdown of the same technique and conditions.  Put your money where your mouth is. ', '2007-04-25 01:02:36.000000', NULL, 0),
