(3580211, 498425, 68035, '<td valign="top">Yaaay Deb, great photo, great result and not even a train station in sight!!!<br/> <br/>I think the fields of yellow stuff that you mention are crops of rapeseed oil, which for the last ten years or so have been appearing everywhere (can be used for producing vegetable oil for people and biodiesel amongst other things but is a real killer if you get too near it and you suffer from hayfever)<br/> <br/>Anyway enough of the natural biology lesson, congrats again for a beautiful image<br/> <br/></td>', 'Yaaay Deb, great photo, great result and not even a train station in sight!!! I think the fields of yellow stuff that you mention are crops of rapeseed oil, which for the last ten years or so have been appearing everywhere (can be used for producing vegetable oil for people and biodiesel amongst other things but is a real killer if you get too near it and you suffer from hayfever) Anyway enough of the natural biology lesson, congrats again for a beautiful image ', '2007-04-25 04:33:02.000000', NULL, 0),
