(3581185, 499057, 50583, '<td valign="top">WOOT!! Thanks for all the comments!! I was kind of expecting a little better score out of this one but once again my lack of experience in post-processing hurt me a bit.  At least I have a new image on my profile! :)</td>', 'WOOT!! Thanks for all the comments!! I was kind of expecting a little better score out of this one but once again my lack of experience in post-processing hurt me a bit.  At least I have a new image on my profile! :)', '2007-04-25 11:58:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3581203, 498327, 30049, '<td valign="top">Judi - I think you used Photoshop quite well on this.  It''s a wonderful piece of art.  However, that being said, I also think this seems too much like a digital graphic that goes over the edge of maintaining photographic integrity.<br/> <br/>You had a wide range of votes on this and I think the DPC community is still trying to decide whether ''Expert Editing'' is a good fit for what''s been more or less fairly traditional photography for the past several years.<br/> <br/>I pulled the following quote from the <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_rules.php?RULES_ID=14" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Expert Editing (Trial)</a> Challenge Rules.<br/> <br/>"You are encouraged to keep your entries photographic in nature, and voters are encouraged to rate entries accordingly."<br/> <br/>Obviously this is JMO, and I''m one of those old-fashioned conservative types.  :P</td>', 'Judi - I think you used Photoshop quite well on this.  It''s a wonderful piece of art.  However, that being said, I also think this seems too much like a digital graphic that goes over the edge of maintaining photographic integrity. You had a wide range of votes on this and I think the DPC community is still trying to decide whether ''Expert Editing'' is a good fit for what''s been more or less fairly traditional photography for the past several years. I pulled the following quote from the Expert Editing (Trial) Challenge Rules. "You are encouraged to keep your entries photographic in nature, and voters are encouraged to rate entries accordingly." Obviously this is JMO, and I''m one of those old-fashioned conservative types.  :P', '2007-04-25 12:02:57.000000', NULL, 0),
