(3582579, 496842, 62095, '<td valign="top">Yeah I think the multiple-exposure HDR is a tricky thing to get right. The slightest variation in camera position or wind-driven movement of the subject will end up knocking out the image in a slight way. I''ve had a few shots that I thought would be good end up messed up by that.<br/> <br/>Having said that I don''t think that this was a disaster by any stretch.  I think, had the perspective been right, I''d have been tempted to have the bird up front right, for some foreground interest.</td>', 'Yeah I think the multiple-exposure HDR is a tricky thing to get right. The slightest variation in camera position or wind-driven movement of the subject will end up knocking out the image in a slight way. I''ve had a few shots that I thought would be good end up messed up by that. Having said that I don''t think that this was a disaster by any stretch.  I think, had the perspective been right, I''d have been tempted to have the bird up front right, for some foreground interest.', '2007-04-25 17:32:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3582608, 498327, 36988, '<td valign="top">So you went all the way with this and caused a bit of a stir for yourself. Not a bad road to travel at all if you ask me. Prompting a response, good or bad is alot better that going unnoticed wouldn''t you say. In the end you''ve got an image that I''m sure kills in full size and demonstrates your ability to present YOUR visions in YOUR way beautifully. In short, you are one who CAN. <br/> <br/>TIHadi<br/> <br/>The volume light is going in too many directions!! The wave should break from behind the girl same direction of the waves. The colors of the sky do not match. poor job of mixing the breaking wave with the clouds above it. <br/>The light on the bird is coming from the wrong direction. <br/>Powerful editing tools in the wrong hands. 1 <br/> <br/>Those that CAN, DO and those that CAN''T... insult and criticize. As I stated earlier, ''Prompting a response, good or bad is alot better than going unnoticed''. Ask Mr. TIHadi to explain that to you... he''s very well acquainted with going unoticed and his opinion has as much impact and depth as his images do. <br/>Powerful editing tool in the wrong hands... perhaps... :P<br/>I''ll take his opinion more seriously when HIS images do more than simply occupy space... and so should YOU!<br/>Rd<br/> <br/></td>', 'So you went all the way with this and caused a bit of a stir for yourself. Not a bad road to travel at all if you ask me. Prompting a response, good or bad is alot better that going unnoticed wouldn''t you say. In the end you''ve got an image that I''m sure kills in full size and demonstrates your ability to present YOUR visions in YOUR way beautifully. In short, you are one who CAN.  TIHadi The volume light is going in too many directions!! The wave should break from behind the girl same direction of the waves. The colors of the sky do not match. poor job of mixing the breaking wave with the clouds above it. The light on the bird is coming from the wrong direction. Powerful editing tools in the wrong hands. 1  Those that CAN, DO and those that CAN''T... insult and criticize. As I stated earlier, ''Prompting a response, good or bad is alot better than going unnoticed''. Ask Mr. TIHadi to explain that to you... he''s very well acquainted with going unoticed and his opinion has as much impact and depth as his images do. Powerful editing tool in the wrong hands... perhaps... :PI''ll take his opinion more seriously when HIS images do more than simply occupy space... and so should YOU!Rd ', '2007-04-25 17:44:48.000000', NULL, 0),
