(3590430, 498503, 70828, '<td valign="top">Okay ... I had great fun with this and think that I made your image better by my PP but that is all personal taste. I have already sent you the high res results of my tweaking and hope you like them. Here you can see what my edit of your image looks like in the same resolution as you submitted it in the first place. You have submitted here a 1.333:1 ratio image but sent me a 1.5 to 1 ratio image.<br/> <br/>I maintained the 1.5:1 ratio because I thought it was better for this photo but cropped it so that the peak of the dark rock was at the LH Rule of Thirds line. I also noticed that it has some highlights leading lines going for it with this crop ... (accidental but I like it) and I cloned out the tiny branch up against said rock on the left to not distract from it.<br/> <br/>I hope you like what I did.<br/> <br/>Detailed description of editing to follow as soon as I type out my hand written notes.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=504129" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504129.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504129.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504129.jpg"/></a> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=504130" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504130.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504130.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504130.jpg"/></a> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=504132" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504132.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504132.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504132.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Thank you SO much for letting me play with your capture ... :)<br/> <br/>I dunno about anyone else ... but this image makes me jealous that I did not get a chance to scramble up here and YOU did.<br/> <br/>OK here are my editing steps ... <br/> <br/>-Cropped as described above<br/>-Increase Dynamic Range using screen and multiply adjustment layers as per this tutorial <a href="//dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=20" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=20</a> <br/>-Noise reduction filter Strength 1, Reduce Color Noise 100<br/>-Levels - Push midranges to 1.3<br/>-Curves - Slight S-Curve to increase contrast<br/>-Clone out distracting LH branch<br/>-Resize back to 3072 X 2048 (for the one to email you)<br/>-Resize to 720 X 480 (for here)<br/>-Selective Color - Cyans and Blues +20 black<br/>-Saturation +20<br/>-USM 50% @2.0 pixels, 10 levels<br/> <br/>... and here is the same image I edited above tone mapped a touch for EXTRA pop!<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=504496" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504496.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504496.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70828/thumb/504496.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-04-29 06:59:25.</i></td>', 'Okay ... I had great fun with this and think that I made your image better by my PP but that is all personal taste. I have already sent you the high res results of my tweaking and hope you like them. Here you can see what my edit of your image looks like in the same resolution as you submitted it in the first place. You have submitted here a 1.333:1 ratio image but sent me a 1.5 to 1 ratio image. I maintained the 1.5:1 ratio because I thought it was better for this photo but cropped it so that the peak of the dark rock was at the LH Rule of Thirds line. I also noticed that it has some highlights leading lines going for it with this crop ... (accidental but I like it) and I cloned out the tiny branch up against said rock on the left to not distract from it. I hope you like what I did. Detailed description of editing to follow as soon as I type out my hand written notes.     Thank you SO much for letting me play with your capture ... :) I dunno about anyone else ... but this image makes me jealous that I did not get a chance to scramble up here and YOU did. OK here are my editing steps ...  -Cropped as described above-Increase Dynamic Range using screen and multiply adjustment layers as per this tutorial //dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=20 -Noise reduction filter Strength 1, Reduce Color Noise 100-Levels - Push midranges to 1.3-Curves - Slight S-Curve to increase contrast-Clone out distracting LH branch-Resize back to 3072 X 2048 (for the one to email you)-Resize to 720 X 480 (for here)-Selective Color - Cyans and Blues +20 black-Saturation +20-USM 50% @2.0 pixels, 10 levels ... and here is the same image I edited above tone mapped a touch for EXTRA pop! ', '2007-04-28 14:39:45.000000', '2007-04-29 07:59:25.000000', 0),
